# Board variant: the driver uses the real I2C bus instead of the
# simulated registers. Build it in its OWN build directory, so the
# QEMU build in build/ stays as it is (from this project directory):
#
#   idf.py -B build-hw -D SDKCONFIG=build-hw/sdkconfig \
#       -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hw" build
#   idf.py -B build-hw -D SDKCONFIG=build-hw/sdkconfig -p <port> \
#       flash monitor
#
# (The defaults only apply when an sdkconfig is created, and idf.py
# remembers the list in the build directory -- so in build/ this layer
# would be silently ignored.) Not usable in QEMU, which has no I2C bus.
# CONFIG_LAB3_REG_SIM is not set
